On 20/05/2010 13:09, Gilles Chanteperdrix wrote:
> Ramon wrote:
>    
>> Hi,
>>
>> I would like to begin using xenomai (I have no previous experience with it).
>> I would like to know which is the best linux distribution to begin with
>> it (the distribution
>> contains all needed libraries and correct compilator versions ...).
>>
>> Any suggestion ?
>>      
> On what system do you intend to run Xenomai? On a desktop system? Or an
> embedded board?
>
> If a desktop system, I bet the simplest choice are dpkg based
> distributions such as Debian or Ubuntu, since Xenomai exists as a Debian
> package. But there are no needed libraries (except the C library) and
> all gcc versions able to compile the Linux kernel should be supported.
> So, if you plan to compile Xenomai yourself, all distributions are equal.
>
>    
Yes ... by now I'm using a Desktop machine.

Thank you
Ramon

